cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "Gazetteer of the World → Linked Data: an OCR-to-linked-data pipeline for the 1856 RGS Gazetteer"
abstract: >-
  A documented pipeline turning a 19th-century printed gazetteer into a
  structured, AAT-typed, geolocated authority gazetteer for the World
  Historical Gazetteer. The source is the Royal Geographical Society's
  "A Gazetteer of the World, or Dictionary of Geographical Knowledge"
  (Edinburgh: A. Fullarton & Co., 1856), 7 vols. Public-domain first-edition
  page images are OCRed with a layout-aware model (Surya) on a GPU cluster,
  parsed into per-record entries with page-level provenance, typed against
  validated Getty AAT identifiers via LLM extraction, and reconciled against
  the WHG index. Note that the working pipeline depends on University of
  Pittsburgh CRC infrastructure (Slurm + vLLM) and WHG's Elasticsearch
  gateway, so it is not turn-key reproducible outside that environment; it is
  best read as a thoroughly documented record of how this gazetteer was
  digitised and ingested, and as a design reference for comparable
  infrastructure.
type: software
